L4-E4: BOARD A'S CURRENT-LIMIT COORDINATION (U3 IIN_HOST, R11) AND THE OUTLET'S TRIP (R138) (l4e4_limits.py,
MESHSAT-1357). PROTOTYPE DESIGN: nothing bought, built, powered or measured; no generator, registry or page edited.
Basis per figure: MAKER (document, page), NETLIST, MODELED, INFERRED (method stated), ASSUMPTION; INCONCLUSIVE where no
held document gives the figure.

0. REPRODUCTIONS (refused, exit 4, if either fails)
   0a r11_dep.py re-run in a child process reproduces r11_dep.out byte for byte (sha256/16 f9d2c6f23fab3edc): yes
   0b r11_dep.main() run in this process, its locals taken at return, prints the same bytes: yes; every figure below
      that r11_dep.py computes (VSNS, the ISNS offset, R11's tolerance and TCR, U3's accuracy, the other loads, the
      temperatures, the stage relations, the bands) is taken from that run, not retyped
   pinned: r11_dep.py 6636a7489d3d1406, l4e_replay.out 59c6eeab16da98f8; board A's netlist sha256/16 6c40250c47195ebb (r11_dep.py's 14 facts hold on it)

1. U3's IIN_HOST FOR REQ-016's 100 W WINDOW
   what the window needs at VBUS20 (MODELED, l4e_replay.out 8; the lowest bus 19.146 V), with the records' INFERRED 0.10 A
   between a setting and U3's minimum (C-7), and U3's maximum by r11_dep.py's rule (the larger of SLUSE66A p.80's
   100 mA and p.1's +-2.5 %), plus C-9's 0.079 A of VBUS20's other loads through R11 (r11_dep.out 3, four FETs switching):
     declared     0.93 x 0.93: 86.5 W, U3's minimum at least 4.517 A -> setting 4.65 A, its maximum 4.766 A, through R11 4.845 A
     high bracket 0.97 x 0.97: 94.1 W, U3's minimum at least 4.914 A -> setting 5.05 A, its maximum 5.176 A, through R11 5.255 A
     no loss      1.00 x 1.00: 100.0 W, U3's minimum at least 5.223 A -> setting 5.35 A, its maximum 5.484 A, through R11 5.563 A
     (l4e_replay.out 8 prints 4.829 / 5.229 / 5.529 A through R11 with the 100 mA alone; p.1's 2.5 % is the larger above 4 A,
     so the coordination here uses 4.845 A for the chosen setting)
   CHOSEN: IIN_HOST 4.65 A. Reason: the declared efficiencies are the only figures this tree holds for the stage and the
     front end (C-8 open, no maker figure); the 0.97 bracket is a sensitivity no document establishes. At 4.65 A U3's
     INFERRED minimum 4.55 A carries all the window gives at the declared figures (4.517 A), and the corrected path's
     result is unchanged (MODELED, l4e_replay.out 8: A2 window-sized 286.3 / 516.5 Wh unserved at 48 / 72 h, the same as the
     drafted 6.2 A's 286.3 / 516.5 Wh). A higher setting asks more than the declared window gives, which is A-2's collapse case;
     raising it to 5.05 A is a firmware step only once C-8's bench figures reach the bracket, and needs R11 at 7 mOhm (2 below)
   REGISTER (MAKER SLUSE66A p.80, 9.6.22 and Figure 9-35): R16 is 10mOhm 1% 2512 (NETLIST), so RSNS_RAC = 0b (p.25, 9.3.5,
     'if 10-mOhm sensing is used please configure RSNS_RAC=0b'; the POR default is 5 mOhm); the 10 mOhm range is 50 to 6350 mA
     with 50 mA resolution, a 7-bit code in bits 14:8: code 93 (0x5D), REG0x0F/0E() = 0x5D00; nominal 4.65 A; maximum
     nominal + 100 mA = 4.750 A (p.80), +2.5 % = 4.766 A (p.1); carried 4.766 A. The host writes it again after every
     adapter removal, which resets IIN_HOST to 3.25 A (p.26, 9.3.6): A-2's startup rule
   TI's accuracy (MAKER SLUSE66A): p.1 '+-2.5 % input current regulation' (a feature line, no conditions); p.10, 8.5
     Electrical Characteristics, IIN_DPM_REG_ACC over -40 to 105 C, rows only for the 5 mOhm RAC: 7.8 A: 7.6 to 8.0 A; 5.8 A: 5.6 to 6.0 A; 2.8 A: 2.6 to 3.0 A; 0.8 A: 0.6 to 1.0 A
     (+-0.2 A, that is +-1 mV of sense voltage); no row is printed for the 10 mOhm RAC
   C-7, U3's input-current MINIMUM at 4.65 A: INCONCLUSIVE. No TI figure is held for the 10 mOhm RAC. Carried: the records'
     INFERRED 0.10 A margin, 4.55 A (consistent with p.10's +-1 mV over 10 mOhm and with p.80's 100 mA / 200 mA pair for
     10 / 5 mOhm, INFERRED); read on p.1's 2.5 % it would be 4.534 A, still at or above the 4.517 A the window needs
     (+0.017 A). Closure (the page's): the bench reading at or above 4.55 A

2. R11, THE LM5176 U2's AVERAGE-CURRENT SENSE (SNVSAI1D p.17 Equation 4, ICL(AVG) = VSNS / RSNS; VSNS 43 / 50 / 57 mV p.7)
   the stacked band, r11_dep.py's own band(): VSNS minimum less the ISNS offset 0.3 mV, R11 +1 % and its TCR 50 ppm/K
     over r11_dep.py's 75 K envelope (R11 between -20 C and the ASSUMED 100 C). Must exceed 4.845 A (U3 at 4.65 A, its maximum
     4.766 A, plus 0.079 A). C-1's tap allowance by r11_dep.py's margin rule; the page accepted 0.29 mOhm at 25 C for 6.2 mOhm
   the held part's catalogue family (JLCPCB's public search for HoJLR2512-3W, jlc-search-hojlr2512-3w-2026-10-01.json; 1 %, 3 W, in stock, 5 to 10 mOhm):
     HoJLR2512-3W-5mR-1%    C2903482 stock 106666: band 8.424 / 10.000 / 11.619 A; taps at most +3.744 mOhm working, +2.891 mOhm at 25 C: eligible
     HoJLR2512-3W-6mR-1%    C2904238 stock   5536: band 7.020 / 8.333 / 9.683 A; taps at most +2.730 mOhm working, +2.108 mOhm at 25 C: eligible
     HoJLR2512-3W-7mR-1%    C2904239 stock   1833: band 6.017 / 7.143 / 8.300 A; taps at most +1.716 mOhm working, +1.325 mOhm at 25 C: eligible
     HoJLR2512-3W-8mR-1%    C2904240 stock   9630: band 5.265 / 6.250 / 7.262 A; taps at most +0.702 mOhm working, +0.542 mOhm at 25 C: eligible
     HoJLR2512-3W-9mR-1%    C2904241 stock   2938: band 4.680 / 5.556 / 6.455 A; taps at most -0.312 mOhm working, -0.241 mOhm at 25 C: not eligible
     HoJLR2512-3W-10mR-1%   C2903468 stock 136379: band 4.212 / 5.000 / 5.810 A; taps at most -1.325 mOhm working, -1.024 mOhm at 25 C: not eligible
   CHOSEN: R11 8 mOhm, HoJLR2512-3W-8mR-1%, LCSC C2904240 (Milliohm; LCSC's answer 2026-10-01T02:58Z: ±1%, ±50ppm/℃, 3W; its datasheet link returns the held
     series sheet byte for byte, sha256/16 3224518dbc8bdc85, so C-2's 'its sheet filed' holds: MAKER HoJLR2512 p.1 F = +-1 %, 3 W for
     0.5 to 500 mOhm; p.2 TCR +-50 ppm/K for 2 to 500 mOhm). Rule: the LARGEST eligible value, because the band's maximum,
     the highest permitted current that B-1, B-2 and B-4 must be closed at, falls as R11 rises; 9 mOhm leaves no tap budget
   per temperature (R11's own temperature from the air to the air plus 17.3 K, its rise at the band minimum's 5.265 A with
     the output ripple all through R11, 0.52 W, by the derating line's 33.3 K/W, INFERRED as r11_dep.py; TCR on the larger
     excursion from 25 C; copper of the taps at the upper end, 0.00393 /K):
     air      R11 C     stacked min, R11 alone             with kelvin_check's 1 % per tap    with C-1's full allowance         
      -20.0 C -20.0..-2.7 5.273 A, margin +0.427 A           5.182 A, margin +0.336 A           4.976 A, margin +0.130 A
       25.0 C 25.0..42.3 5.280 A, margin +0.435 A           5.171 A, margin +0.325 A           4.927 A, margin +0.082 A
       62.1 C 62.1..79.4 5.270 A, margin +0.425 A           5.147 A, margin +0.302 A           4.874 A, margin +0.029 A
     every margin over U3's maximum plus 0.079 A is positive at all three; at r11_dep.py's 75 K envelope the stacked
     minimum of R11 alone is 5.265 A, margin +0.420 A, which C-1's allowance is defined to take whole
   C-1 RECOMPUTED (r11_dep.py's margin rule at 8 mOhm and 4.845 A): the copper R11's current shares with the two taps, both
     together, at most 0.702 mOhm at its working temperature; 0.613 mOhm at 25 C with the copper at 62.1 C and 0.542 mOhm with it
     at 100 C: the criterion is 0.54 mOhm at 25 C (it was 0.29 for 6.2 mOhm). kelvin_check's own 1 % per tap (0.16 mOhm for
     both) is stricter and closes it too. Bench 7b.3: the DC voltage across U2 pins 14 and 13 exceeds I x R11 (four-wire)
     by at most 0.54 mOhm x I (2.63 mV at 4.845 A)
   R11's DISSIPATION at 4.845 A (in service): 0.190 W DC (I2R at +1 %); with the output ripple all through R11 (an upper
     bound) 0.262 W at 15.1 V and 0.440 W at 9.0 V in (r11_dep.py's stage relations). Its own temperature (INFERRED, 33.3 K/W):
     -20.0 C air: -13.7 C DC, -5.3 C upper bound, rating derated to 3.00 W; 25.0 C air: 31.3 C DC, 39.7 C upper bound, rating derated to 3.00 W; 62.1 C air: 68.4 C DC, 76.8 C upper bound, rating derated to 2.80 W
     (MAKER p.2: 3 W derated from 70 C to 0 at 170 C). Rated current sqrt(P/R) 19.4 A (p.3); the ASSUMED 100 C of r11_dep.py holds
   sensitivity, not stacked by r11_dep.py's rule: the series' load-life drift (MAKER p.4, < +-1 % after 1000 h at rated power
     and 70 C) added as a further +1 % leaves the 75 K envelope's R11-alone margin at +0.367 A
   carried to item 4 (fault handling; INFERRED by r11_dep.py's relations, nothing decided here): the band's maximum, the
     highest permitted current, 7.262 A (held 10 mOhm 5.810 A, the drafted 6.2 mOhm 9.370 A); L1's peak at 9 V there 20.74 A
     with Isat's 30 % drop on the -20 % tolerance, against the typical Isat 17.5 A; VBUS20's worst can scaled 2.69 A matched,
     3.11 A at a 2:1 ESR spread, against 2.8 A a can (B-4 stays open at 2:1 unless hiccup bounds the fault, B-2)
   NOT CHOSEN: the 0.97 bracket's 5.05 A (5.255 A through R11) would need HoJLR2512-3W-7mR-1% (C2904239): band 6.017 / 7.143 / 8.300 A, taps 0.79 mOhm
     at 25 C; its highest permitted current is 8.300 A, 1.037 A above the chosen R11's; 8 mOhm leaves 0.011 mOhm for the taps
     there, so the bracket is a hardware change (R11 and the fault closures), not a register write

3. R138, THE USB-C OUTLET'S OCP SENSE (DR-03), TPS25740A U18
   NETLIST: R138 '10mOhm 1% 2512 (ISNS)' from PD_SW (U18 pin 19 ISNS, Q27's source) to PD_VBUS (U18 pin 21 VBUS, J_USBC_OUT pin 1);
     straps: HIPWR (pin 5) on PD_DVDD, EN9V (pin 8) on GND, PSEL (pin 12) on PD_DVDD, PCTRL (pin 14) on PD_VAUX
   the PDO table (MAKER SLVSDG8B): Table 2 p.28, EN9V low and HIPWR direct, 5, 9 and 15 V; Equation 2 p.28, HIPWR high,
     Imax = 3 A, PCTRL high, Pmax = P(SEL) = 93 W (Table 3, PSEL direct to DVDD); Table 5 p.29 (TPS25740A, the 3 A block),
     PSEL direct to DVDD, PCTRL high: 5 V 3.0 A, 9 V 3.0 A, 15 V 3.0 A; 8.3.6 p.28: a non-PD Type-C sink is
     offered 15 W, 3.0 A at 5 V. Every row of Table 5's 3 A block is at most 3.0 A (l3batt's 18 W straps among them).
     The generator declares the same: U18 '5, 9, 15 V at 3 A', _PD_A 3.0 A (gen_sch_a.py). Largest PDO current 3.0 A
   TI's recommendation: 5 mOhm (p.31, 8.3.8.2: at 3 A via HIPWR 'the OCP threshold lies between 3.8 A and 4.5 A'; p.49,
     9.2.4.2.3, the 5, 9 and 15 V at 3 A example: 'targeted towards a 5 mOhm, +-1 % sense resistor', 45 mW at 3 A)
   CHOSEN: R138 5 mOhm, HoJLR2512-3W-5mR-1%, LCSC C2903482 (Milliohm; LCSC's answer 2026-10-01T02:58Z: ±1%, 3W; its datasheet link returns the held HoJLR2512
     series sheet byte for byte: MAKER p.1 F = +-1 %, p.2 TCR +-50 ppm/K). Board A's other 5 mOhm parts are LR2512D-3W-5mR-1%
     C500739, whose maker sheet is not held (gen_sch_a.py); the held sheet's part is named so the window rests on MAKER figures
   VI(TRIP) (MAKER p.11, 7.5, V(ISNS) - V(VBUS), -40 to 125 C): 19.2 to 22.6 mV 'HIPWR: 5 A not enabled'; 29 to 34 mV
     'HIPWR = DVDD (5 A enabled)'. That label contradicts Tables 4 and 5, Equation 2 and 8.3.6, where HIPWR to DVDD is the
     3 A configuration (l3batt CHECK-3 minor 1 found the same); p.31 ties the 3.8 to 4.5 A threshold to the 3 A configuration
     and to 5 mOhm, which is 19.2 to 22.6 mV over 5 mOhm. Taken: the 3 A row (INFERRED from p.29 and p.31 together)
   R138's temperature: the air from -20 to 62.1 C plus 3.5 K of its own (its trip maximum's I2R, 33.3 K/W INFERRED); TCR over
     45.0 K from 25 C
   TRIP WINDOW at 5 mOhm (+-1 %, TCR): 3.793 to 4.576 A. Above every PDO: 5 V 3.0 A +0.793 A; 9 V 3.0 A +0.793 A; 15 V 3.0 A +0.793 A;
     the non-PD 5 V 3.0 A +0.793 A. (As drawn, 10 mOhm: 1.897 to 2.288 A, below every 3 A contract: DR-03 reproduced)
   below the ratings of what it protects (the trip maximum 4.576 A):
     R138 itself: rated current sqrt(3 W / 5 mOhm) 24.5 A (MAKER HoJLR2512 p.1, p.3); 0.045 W at 3 A, 0.106 W at the trip maximum
     Q27 CSD18510Q5B (NETLIST, the VBUS switch the trip opens): 42 A continuous (MAKER SLPS632 p.1, note 1: TA 25 C, 1 in2 2 oz)
     the wall receptacle, Bulgin PXP4043/C (CASE-MARGINS.md): 5 A (MAKER Bulgin 4000 series sheet p.3, 'Current rating'):
       below, +0.424 A
     board A's J_USBC_OUT 'wall USB-C outlet, power only (pigtail header)': no part number, no maker
       rating held: INCONCLUSIVE (its VBUS is one 2.54 mm pin carrying the whole outlet current)
     the user's cable: no rating held (no e-marker is read; 8.3.6 p.28 caps the advertisement at 3 A for that reason): not judged
   if the p.11 label were right (29 to 34 mV with HIPWR on DVDD), the window would be 5.730 to 6.884 A: above the receptacle's
     5 A. The bench must therefore find the trip current itself, not only a 3 A load without a trip
   the stage ahead (U19, R81 10 mOhm, r11_dep.py's band at 10 mOhm, INFERRED for R81): 4.212 / 5.000 / 5.810 A; above every PDO,
     overlapping the trip's upper end: in an overload between them the stage limits, VBUS falls, and p.31 treats VBUS below
     V(VBUS_FTH) as an OCP event
   R138's taps (INFERRED, C-1's margin rule applied to U18): the copper R138's current shares with ISNS and VBUS at most
     1.34 mOhm at its working temperature, 1.15 mOhm at 25 C, for the trip minimum to stay at or above 3.0 A; pcb_sensitive.yaml
     declares no R138 tap today (a layout item for the generator owner)

