5. INCONCLUSIVE, AND WHAT THE BENCH MUST STILL SHOW
   INCONCLUSIVE: C-7 (U3's minimum for the 10 mOhm RAC; carried 0.10 A INFERRED); J_USBC_OUT's pin rating (no part); which
     VI(TRIP) row board A's strap selects (the maker's own label conflict); R11's actual temperature (the 100 C stays an
     ASSUMPTION; the INFERRED rise is the derating line's, no thermal resistance printed); the undocumented efficiencies (C-8)
   bench 7b.1: the front end's CC onset with an electronic load past U3, at -20, 25 and 62 C: above 4.845 A at each
   bench 7b.3: R11's Kelvin error, at most 0.54 mOhm x I at 25 C
   C-7: U3's input current at the 4.65 A setting read at or above 4.55 A
   the outlet: a 3 A load on each PDO (5, 9, 15 V and the non-PD 5 V) held without a trip; then the trip current itself
     by a slow ramp, inside 3.79 to 4.58 A (it would read about 5.7 to 6.9 A on the p.11 label's reading)

END. Desk figures on the makers' pages, the committed netlist and the reproduced records; nothing measured or implemented.
